1
00:00:00,116 --> 00:00:01,116
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,116 --> 00:00:02,116
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,116 --> 00:00:04,083
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:04,083 --> 00:00:07,283
[Episode 6]

5
00:00:11,764 --> 00:00:14,583
Just how far is he going?

6
00:00:18,032 --> 00:00:19,876
I've been here before.

7
00:00:19,876 --> 00:00:21,524
What? When?

8
00:00:21,524 --> 00:00:23,449
Where is this place, Mr. Kwon?

9
00:00:27,252 --> 00:00:29,220
Wait, a casino?

10
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:32,280
Chairman Cheon came to a casino
at a time like this?

11
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:35,949
When two people just died
at his construction site?

12
00:00:48,164 --> 00:00:50,783
Chairman, I'm Kwon Tae Seong
from Not Today. I requested an interview.

13
00:00:50,783 --> 00:00:52,683
Wait, just a moment...

14
00:00:53,672 --> 00:00:55,005
Why are you covering my mouth?

15
00:00:55,005 --> 00:00:56,356
Chairman! Just a moment.

16
00:00:56,356 --> 00:00:58,825
Wait, Chairman!

17
00:00:58,825 --> 00:01:00,083
Just a moment.

18
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:02,349
Just let me in for a moment!

19
00:01:04,016 --> 00:01:05,404
I told you to stop.

20
00:01:05,404 --> 00:01:07,116
Stay put.

21
00:01:19,108 --> 00:01:20,192
Are you okay, Mr. Kwon?

22
00:01:20,192 --> 00:01:21,360
Yeah. You got it, right?

23
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:23,496
Oh, yes, I got it.

24
00:01:23,496 --> 00:01:26,168
Still, it was worth following him
all the way here.

25
00:01:26,168 --> 00:01:29,560
Just coming to a casino
at a time like this is newsworthy.

26
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:32,232
- That's not enough, though, huh?
- What?

27
00:01:32,232 --> 00:01:35,216
Not everyone at a casino is there to gamble.

28
00:01:35,216 --> 00:01:36,916
We need to catch him actually gambling,

29
00:01:36,916 --> 00:01:39,264
or at least meet him
and get a few words out of him.

30
00:01:39,264 --> 00:01:40,964
We came all this way for this.

31
00:01:43,196 --> 00:01:44,196
But how are we supposed to do that?

32
00:01:44,196 --> 00:01:47,132
They don't even look like they'll let us
take one step inside, do they?

33
00:01:47,132 --> 00:01:49,183
Is this the only way in?

34
00:01:53,284 --> 00:01:55,383
<i>Go through the lobby,
pass the bell desk on the left,</i>

35
00:01:55,383 --> 00:01:57,649
<i>and open the door on the right.</i>

36
00:01:59,284 --> 00:02:01,916
<i>There should be a staff-only elevator.</i>

37
00:02:07,149 --> 00:02:09,583
<i>Take it to the maid's room on B3</i>

38
00:02:10,332 --> 00:02:12,716
and get a master key for the rooms.

39
00:02:14,624 --> 00:02:16,096
Could I ask you a favor?

40
00:02:16,096 --> 00:02:18,083
Of course, I have to help.

41
00:02:18,083 --> 00:02:21,740
You're investigating a case
involving an unjust death, after all.

42
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:27,228
Your article helped us a lot when we were
fighting wrongful dismissal last year.

43
00:02:27,228 --> 00:02:30,252
Come this way, through the back door.
Come with me.

44
00:02:33,588 --> 00:02:35,683
Excuse me.

45
00:02:37,783 --> 00:02:39,916
<i>Doors closing.</i>

46
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,232
What floor?

47
00:02:45,232 --> 00:02:47,680
B3, the parking garage.

48
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,549
This is for staff only.

49
00:02:49,549 --> 00:02:53,716
You'll have to go back up to the first floor
and take the elevator outside.

50
00:02:53,716 --> 00:02:55,383
Oh, okay. Got it. I'm sorry.

51
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:57,083
Oh, okay.

52
00:03:01,276 --> 00:03:03,949
<i>Doors closing.</i>

53
00:03:11,104 --> 00:03:12,684
Looks like you won't
need to go to the maid room.

54
00:03:12,684 --> 00:03:15,216
Just go straight up to the 23rd floor.

55
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:23,449
Reporting with you...

56
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:26,349
is always thrilling.

57
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:32,483
You'll get used to it eventually.

58
00:03:33,235 --> 00:03:36,649
<i>It seems like it'll be
hard to go up unnoticed.</i>

59
00:03:36,649 --> 00:03:40,483
There are two maids on B1
and two more on the first floor.

60
00:03:40,483 --> 00:03:42,083
Just avoid showing your face
as much as possible.

61
00:03:42,083 --> 00:03:43,316
I'll delete the footage right away.

62
00:03:43,316 --> 00:03:45,049
<i>Okay.</i>

63
00:04:10,636 --> 00:04:13,249
- <i>Doors closing.</i>
- Why is it so exhausting today?

64
00:04:13,992 --> 00:04:15,183
I don't know why there's
so much going on today.

65
00:04:15,183 --> 00:04:17,060
Seriously, why is there so darn much work?

66
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:18,760
I'm exhausted.

67
00:04:19,688 --> 00:04:22,816
Oh? You're VIP guests.

68
00:04:22,816 --> 00:04:25,392
Oh, I think you got on the wrong elevator.

69
00:04:25,392 --> 00:04:26,616
What?

70
00:04:26,616 --> 00:04:30,016
Next time, use the VIP elevator
on the other side of the hall.

71
00:04:30,016 --> 00:04:32,283
This one's for staff.

72
00:04:32,283 --> 00:04:34,336
Oh, I see.

73
00:04:34,336 --> 00:04:36,456
Thank you.

74
00:04:36,456 --> 00:04:38,156
You too, ma'am.

75
00:04:49,849 --> 00:04:52,349
[Yul's Daycare]

76
00:05:11,464 --> 00:05:14,283
Excuse me, I'm getting off.

77
00:05:29,424 --> 00:05:31,968
What's wrong?

78
00:05:31,968 --> 00:05:34,228
Huh?

79
00:05:34,228 --> 00:05:35,536
Never mind.

80
00:05:35,536 --> 00:05:37,949
Her back just looked like someone.

81
00:05:39,112 --> 00:05:40,320
What a crazy punk.

82
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:42,916
No, I mean, me.

83
00:05:48,672 --> 00:05:50,964
Yes, Miss. How are you?

84
00:05:50,964 --> 00:05:54,372
Sorry, I couldn't answer your call.
What is it about?

85
00:05:54,372 --> 00:05:56,520
<i>Oh, it's nothing serious.</i>

86
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:59,160
I'm calling about Yul's first-semester
parent consultation.

87
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:02,492
<i>You didn't reply in the app to let us know</i>

88
00:06:02,492 --> 00:06:05,206
whether you'd prefer a phone
or in-person consultation.

89
00:06:05,206 --> 00:06:10,672
Oh, sorry. I missed that.
Well, I'll do the in-person consultation.

90
00:06:10,672 --> 00:06:13,883
<i>Yes, thank you, Miss. Yes.</i>

91
00:06:17,916 --> 00:06:20,860
Yeah, I'll take the stairs from here.

92
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,864
<i>Watch for anyone coming in.</i>

93
00:06:22,864 --> 00:06:24,768
We can't have any more witnesses.

94
00:06:24,768 --> 00:06:27,416
Okay, Ms. Yoo, I'll keep a close watch.

95
00:06:34,196 --> 00:06:36,249
How can I help you?

96
00:06:36,249 --> 00:06:39,260
Are you here as a guest?

97
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:42,660
I'm not here to gamble.
I'm here to meet someone.

98
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:44,583
Who are you looking for?

99
00:06:45,186 --> 00:06:48,283
Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
of Gaecheon Construction is inside, right?

100
00:06:50,022 --> 00:06:52,600
Did you make an appointment?

101
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:55,116
He'll know me if you tell him Kwon Tae Seong.

102
00:06:55,814 --> 00:06:59,151
<i>There are guards stationed
on every floor of the VIP rooms.</i>

103
00:06:59,151 --> 00:07:01,976
<i>When I give you the signal,
come out and move to the left.</i>

104
00:07:01,976 --> 00:07:03,676
Okay.

105
00:07:08,692 --> 00:07:10,392
Now!

106
00:07:15,716 --> 00:07:17,783
When's the next shift coming?

107
00:07:36,592 --> 00:07:38,748
I'm in.

108
00:07:38,748 --> 00:07:40,448
This is a nice room.

109
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:43,583
Wow, what a view.

110
00:07:44,916 --> 00:07:46,543
<i>It's annoying, right?</i>

111
00:07:46,543 --> 00:07:48,248
A guy who should be in a prison cell.

112
00:07:48,248 --> 00:07:50,116
I'll head over to the fridge.

113
00:08:19,364 --> 00:08:20,688
- Done.
- Put it back in the fridge

114
00:08:20,688 --> 00:08:22,349
and take everything else out.

115
00:08:22,349 --> 00:08:25,108
Just leave that one bottle of water.

116
00:08:25,108 --> 00:08:27,560
<i>I saw on social media that Tak Jong Gu
is an "iced drink till I die" guy.</i>

117
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:31,149
What's that?
Something like "a punch in the face"?

118
00:08:33,484 --> 00:08:35,592
Well, that's not bad either.

119
00:08:35,592 --> 00:08:39,149
<i>It means he only drinks iced beverages.</i>

120
00:08:46,248 --> 00:08:47,948
Done.

121
00:08:50,548 --> 00:08:52,248
I'm heading out.

122
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:55,883
<i>Wait, Ms. Yoo.</i>

123
00:08:57,460 --> 00:09:00,016
Someone's coming down the hall.

124
00:09:00,016 --> 00:09:01,816
<i>Looks like guests.</i>

125
00:09:01,816 --> 00:09:05,100
One man and one woman.

126
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,800
It's Tak Jong Gu.

127
00:09:09,736 --> 00:09:11,660
That woman is...

128
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:13,783
Huh? A liquor bottle?

129
00:09:15,712 --> 00:09:17,612
First time somewhere this fancy?

130
00:09:17,612 --> 00:09:19,312
Yeah.

131
00:09:20,228 --> 00:09:22,468
Come on in.

132
00:09:22,468 --> 00:09:25,616
- This is my room.
- Wow!

133
00:09:27,136 --> 00:09:29,916
This room is incredible.

134
00:09:32,116 --> 00:09:34,752
You really were born
to the right parents, huh?

135
00:09:34,752 --> 00:09:38,060
Aren't the rooms...

136
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,876
non-smoking?

137
00:09:39,876 --> 00:09:41,684
What's not allowed?

138
00:09:41,684 --> 00:09:45,032
If anyone acts up,
I can just throw money at them.

139
00:09:45,032 --> 00:09:48,449
Man, the more I see you, the more I like you.

140
00:09:52,112 --> 00:09:54,604
<i>That's the woman. Today's variable.</i>

141
00:09:54,604 --> 00:09:58,020
She's the one who snatched
my VIP pass at the gaming room.

142
00:09:58,020 --> 00:09:59,908
What's the variable this time?

143
00:09:59,908 --> 00:10:01,716
I'm not sure about that either...

144
00:10:01,716 --> 00:10:04,024
<i>He's supposed to be stuck
in the gaming room until dawn.</i>

145
00:10:04,024 --> 00:10:06,049
But why are those two here at this hour...

146
00:10:06,944 --> 00:10:10,816
<i>If you stay hidden there,
I'll find a way to get you out.</i>

147
00:10:15,924 --> 00:10:19,268
Won't they figure out we lied right away?

148
00:10:19,268 --> 00:10:20,716
Well, it's not exactly a lie.

149
00:10:20,716 --> 00:10:24,500
I said he'd know my name.
I never said I had an appointment.

150
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,736
Oh!

151
00:10:25,736 --> 00:10:27,583
Here they come. Smile.

152
00:10:35,216 --> 00:10:38,028
Chairman Cheon says
he has no appointment today.

153
00:10:38,028 --> 00:10:42,632
Oh, really? That's strange.

154
00:10:43,676 --> 00:10:44,872
He must've forgotten.

155
00:10:44,872 --> 00:10:48,583
Instead of standing here,
perhaps I should speak to him in person...

156
00:10:49,576 --> 00:10:53,516
He's already gone to his room to rest,
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

157
00:10:54,472 --> 00:10:56,352
He went in already.

158
00:11:00,228 --> 00:11:03,556
Escort these people downstairs
and tell the gate.

159
00:11:03,556 --> 00:11:07,844
If this happens one more time,
every one of them is getting fired.

160
00:11:07,844 --> 00:11:09,836
Yes, sir.

161
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:11,816
Please come with me.

162
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:19,381
The view is incredible.

163
00:11:19,381 --> 00:11:22,240
It's so wide open. What a view.

164
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:24,284
The wine's good, right?

165
00:11:24,284 --> 00:11:26,636
Huh? I've got some drinks.

166
00:11:26,636 --> 00:11:30,144
Not that cheap stuff. Drink something good.

167
00:11:30,144 --> 00:11:32,472
But you're unique and interesting.

168
00:11:32,472 --> 00:11:34,844
Honestly, you're not my type,

169
00:11:34,844 --> 00:11:36,883
but there's something kind of sexy about you.

170
00:11:39,816 --> 00:11:42,632
If you're here to play,
just play the darn game.

171
00:11:42,632 --> 00:11:44,772
Don't push your luck when you
haven't even been dealt a hand.

172
00:11:44,772 --> 00:11:46,900
Oh?

173
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:49,449
I suddenly feel like
having something greasy, huh?

174
00:11:50,512 --> 00:11:53,883
I can order room service, right?

175
00:11:53,883 --> 00:11:56,267
Order whatever you want.

176
00:11:56,267 --> 00:11:58,116
And strong liquor...

177
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,716
calls for greasy food.

178
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:09,336
Tak Jong Gu just drugged the drink.
Just in case...

179
00:12:09,336 --> 00:12:11,800
<i>No, it's too dangerous for you
to meet him there yourself.</i>

180
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,388
That woman could become a witness,
and we don't even have an escape route yet...

181
00:12:14,388 --> 00:12:15,900
<i>Calm down, Ki Yeong Do.</i>

182
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:18,436
Who's saying I'm meeting him right now?

183
00:12:18,436 --> 00:12:21,309
I'm just saying we need to prevent
anyone from getting hurt.

184
00:12:21,309 --> 00:12:22,920
<i>Well...</i>

185
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:25,749
Maybe just a punch in the face or something?

186
00:12:38,772 --> 00:12:42,348
For their sake, I hope you won't do
anything reckless again.

187
00:12:42,348 --> 00:12:47,316
Of course. What have these people done wrong?
Someone else is guilty.

188
00:12:48,583 --> 00:12:51,349
Then please head back safely.

189
00:12:54,479 --> 00:12:57,349
That young man is almost annoyingly polite.

190
00:12:58,352 --> 00:13:03,449
Oh, we went all the way up there,
only to get kicked out empty-handed.

191
00:13:05,872 --> 00:13:07,904
Not empty-handed.

192
00:13:07,904 --> 00:13:09,660
- What?
- First.

193
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:12,192
Chairman Cheon is
in the VIP gambling room now.

194
00:13:12,192 --> 00:13:14,444
Which means he was gambling.

195
00:13:14,444 --> 00:13:17,360
Chairman Cheon says
he has no appointments today.

196
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,416
Oh, that's right.

197
00:13:19,416 --> 00:13:23,616
He didn't say there was no such person.
He said there was no appointment.

198
00:13:23,616 --> 00:13:26,408
Second, he's in his room right now.

199
00:13:26,408 --> 00:13:29,616
You're not seriously
going to his room, are you?

200
00:13:31,993 --> 00:13:35,316
Wait. Someone else is coming down the hall.

201
00:13:38,757 --> 00:13:40,457
Come in.

202
00:13:46,048 --> 00:13:48,149
What did she order?

203
00:13:54,928 --> 00:13:56,628
Good!

204
00:14:10,776 --> 00:14:13,949
She said she was just washing her hands.
What's taking her so long?

205
00:14:28,856 --> 00:14:30,949
That worked fast, huh?

206
00:14:32,016 --> 00:14:34,040
<i>♪ If you don't come out, I'm busting in ♪</i>

207
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,040
<i>♪ Dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪</i>

208
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,216
<i>♪ If you don't come out, I'm busting in ♪</i>

209
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:44,542
Oh, dear.

210
00:14:44,542 --> 00:14:48,864
Our Jong Gu, Jong Gu, Mr. Tak Jong Gu.

211
00:14:48,864 --> 00:14:51,792
You're not the only one who can use drugs.

212
00:14:51,792 --> 00:14:55,349
He probably never imagined
he'd be the one on the receiving end.

213
00:15:04,804 --> 00:15:06,288
Yeong Do, something's wrong.

214
00:15:06,288 --> 00:15:08,667
<i>What is it? Is it the victim?</i>

215
00:15:08,667 --> 00:15:11,296
No, I think Tak Jong Gu was drugged.

216
00:15:11,296 --> 00:15:12,817
What?

217
00:15:12,817 --> 00:15:14,549
What do you mean...

218
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:19,791
So, should I tell the boss to start?

219
00:15:19,791 --> 00:15:23,236
Not yet. There's something
we need to check first.

220
00:15:23,236 --> 00:15:25,216
There's...

221
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,820
someone in the bathroom.

222
00:15:51,308 --> 00:15:52,308
Who are you?

223
00:15:52,308 --> 00:15:54,833
That's not a kitchen knife.

224
00:15:54,833 --> 00:15:56,533
Are you a hitman?

225
00:16:15,388 --> 00:16:17,220
Yeah, this one's for people.

226
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:18,492
We should at least
introduce ourselves, shouldn't we?

227
00:16:18,492 --> 00:16:19,848
- Do we have to?
- <i>Ms. Yoo, what's going on?</i>

228
00:16:19,848 --> 00:16:22,731
<i>What's happening? Ms. Yoo!</i>

229
00:16:24,044 --> 00:16:25,883
If you don't want to, we can skip it.

230
00:16:25,883 --> 00:16:28,549
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo!

231
00:16:38,491 --> 00:16:40,820
Stay calm. Take it slow.

232
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:42,176
Did she sound like a professional?

233
00:16:42,176 --> 00:16:45,220
Judging by the fact that
she's going up against Ms. Bo Na,

234
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:47,888
she doesn't seem like an ordinary person.

235
00:16:47,888 --> 00:16:50,970
I'll go check out the situation first.

236
00:16:50,970 --> 00:16:52,916
Ms. Yoo's in too much danger.

237
00:16:55,504 --> 00:16:59,583
This is all my fault. I missed my pass.

238
00:16:59,583 --> 00:17:01,284
<i>Calm down.</i>

239
00:17:01,284 --> 00:17:03,884
Director Yoo will be fine.

240
00:17:03,884 --> 00:17:05,291
This won't do.

241
00:17:05,291 --> 00:17:07,372
I'll take out all the CCTV cameras
in the building.

242
00:17:07,372 --> 00:17:11,549
Then the guards will all head
to the gaming room first.

243
00:17:22,255 --> 00:17:24,600
All the CCTV cameras just went down.

244
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:26,988
Perfect timing. Let's start now.

245
00:17:26,988 --> 00:17:28,369
<i>Stand by.</i>

246
00:17:28,369 --> 00:17:30,449
Something just came up over here.

247
00:17:33,633 --> 00:17:35,983
What is taking so long?

248
00:17:39,284 --> 00:17:41,516
You lost?

249
00:18:02,148 --> 00:18:05,049
Looks like there aren't
any security guards here.

250
00:18:05,808 --> 00:18:07,940
That can't be.

251
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:09,816
Could it be shift change?

252
00:18:50,444 --> 00:18:52,256
Huh?

253
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:55,616
Didn't someone just walk past over there?

254
00:19:00,064 --> 00:19:01,483
What are you doing? Let go!

255
00:19:01,483 --> 00:19:04,216
Shh. Just be quiet for a second.

256
00:19:07,204 --> 00:19:10,024
Let's quickly find
Chairman Cheon's room first.

257
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:11,896
Oh, alright.

258
00:19:11,896 --> 00:19:15,049
You said it was the best room
on the 24th floor, right?

259
00:19:16,052 --> 00:19:18,216
Darn it, let go of this!

260
00:19:31,976 --> 00:19:33,676
Shh!

261
00:19:52,244 --> 00:19:56,676
I'm in front of Tak Jong Gu's room.
It's quiet for now.

262
00:19:56,676 --> 00:19:58,483
But I'll go in.

263
00:20:18,316 --> 00:20:23,349
<i>♪ In those four beats, there is love ♪</i>

264
00:20:25,356 --> 00:20:27,216
There's a man too?

265
00:20:36,892 --> 00:20:40,149
He's just passed out from drinking.

266
00:20:40,984 --> 00:20:43,249
And who might you be?

267
00:20:48,724 --> 00:20:51,583
"Death conquers all evil."

268
00:20:51,583 --> 00:20:53,583
That's what our boss always says.

269
00:20:55,872 --> 00:20:59,320
So you guys are behind
what happened to my face?

270
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:02,683
It's only temporary.
The symptoms will subside with time.

271
00:21:02,683 --> 00:21:05,549
You're the local team, aren't you?

272
00:21:07,792 --> 00:21:10,982
Well, things just got interesting.

273
00:21:10,982 --> 00:21:13,083
Are you guys Team A?

274
00:21:16,104 --> 00:21:18,564
It seems our clients have overlapped.

275
00:21:18,564 --> 00:21:20,783
That's never happened before.

276
00:21:22,032 --> 00:21:24,616
This should help ease the symptoms.

277
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:29,384
But "overlap"?

278
00:21:29,384 --> 00:21:31,516
What do you mean?

279
00:21:32,328 --> 00:21:36,149
Isn't Tak Jong Gu your target?

280
00:21:39,488 --> 00:21:41,980
That punk was your target?

281
00:21:41,980 --> 00:21:44,256
No wonder.

282
00:21:44,256 --> 00:21:46,372
He wasn't ours.

283
00:21:46,372 --> 00:21:49,783
- Then...
- Our target is...

284
00:21:51,849 --> 00:21:54,283
Room 2408.

285
00:21:55,192 --> 00:21:56,983
- <i>♪ Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪</i>
- <i>Gaecheon Construction,</i>

286
00:21:56,983 --> 00:22:00,980
- <i>♪ In those four beats ♪</i>
- <i>Chairman Cheon Seong Gil.</i>

287
00:22:00,980 --> 00:22:05,916
<i>♪ There is love, and there are tears ♪</i>

288
00:22:12,052 --> 00:22:13,983
2408.

289
00:22:18,084 --> 00:22:20,683
Well, what a stroke of luck, huh?

290
00:22:20,683 --> 00:22:23,016
You've just made my job easier.

291
00:22:24,032 --> 00:22:27,041
Hey, you, just leave.

292
00:22:27,041 --> 00:22:31,049
I'm letting you live as a special favor
for bringing me here.

293
00:22:32,352 --> 00:22:34,820
- What are you doing?
- Jeez.

294
00:22:34,820 --> 00:22:38,749
That's none of your business,
so leave while I'm letting you walk out.

295
00:22:38,749 --> 00:22:40,284
You don't exactly look

296
00:22:40,284 --> 00:22:43,949
innocent enough to go around
calling yourself a witness,

297
00:22:43,949 --> 00:22:46,544
so I'm letting you go.

298
00:22:46,544 --> 00:22:48,932
I only want to kill one person today.

299
00:22:48,932 --> 00:22:50,632
- Hey!
- Darn it!

300
00:22:55,364 --> 00:22:58,668
Ms. Yoo, can you hear me? Ms. Yoo?

301
00:22:58,668 --> 00:23:00,800
Please, say something! Please!

302
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:01,944
Ms. Yoo!

303
00:23:01,944 --> 00:23:05,349
I need to know why you're trying to kill him.

304
00:23:09,624 --> 00:23:11,088
I gave you a fair chance.

305
00:23:11,088 --> 00:23:12,472
I gave you one too.

306
00:23:12,472 --> 00:23:13,737
Are you a hired killer?

307
00:23:13,737 --> 00:23:15,420
She is with the local team.

308
00:23:15,420 --> 00:23:16,776
Are you listening?

309
00:23:16,776 --> 00:23:19,683
Ms. Yoo, you have to stop, please!

310
00:23:23,536 --> 00:23:25,516
I'm not holding back anymore.

311
00:23:25,516 --> 00:23:26,516
Fine. Go ahead.

312
00:23:26,516 --> 00:23:28,049
Ms. Yoo!

313
00:23:28,049 --> 00:23:30,049
Ms. Yoo, please...

314
00:23:39,664 --> 00:23:43,296
<i>♪ Dun-da, Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪</i>

315
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:47,016
<i>♪ In those four beats ♪</i>

316
00:23:47,016 --> 00:23:50,749
<i>♪ There is love, and there are tears ♪</i>

317
00:23:50,749 --> 00:23:54,684
<i>♪ And there is farewell too ♪</i>

318
00:23:54,684 --> 00:23:57,276
<i>♪ With each verse, each hurdle ♪</i>

319
00:23:57,276 --> 00:24:00,249
<i>♪ When you overcome it ♪</i>

320
00:24:11,768 --> 00:24:14,052
I think this is it, right?

321
00:24:14,052 --> 00:24:17,616
But don't you hear something inside?

322
00:24:43,768 --> 00:24:46,040
Sounds like some guys
horsing around in there.

323
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:48,316
Isn't this the place?

324
00:24:51,032 --> 00:24:53,264
What's going on?

325
00:24:53,264 --> 00:24:55,992
Do you need any help?

326
00:24:55,992 --> 00:24:57,692
No.

327
00:24:59,983 --> 00:25:02,240
I must've gotten the room wrong.

328
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:03,904
I told you it wasn't this room, didn't I?

329
00:25:03,904 --> 00:25:05,915
See? I told you I was right.

330
00:25:05,915 --> 00:25:08,008
- It's upstairs.
- I said it's the floor above.

331
00:25:08,008 --> 00:25:10,972
I've been telling you this whole time.
It's the floor above.

332
00:25:10,972 --> 00:25:13,469
But this is the top floor, though.

333
00:25:13,469 --> 00:25:17,520
<i>Suspicious people are lurking in front of
room 2408, so go check it out.</i>

334
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:19,716
Yeah, I'm going right now.

335
00:25:21,068 --> 00:25:23,952
Wow, we almost got caught.

336
00:25:23,952 --> 00:25:27,248
I thought my heart was going to explode.

337
00:25:27,248 --> 00:25:29,200
I think she's gone.

338
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:31,852
I'm too scared to keep going.

339
00:25:31,852 --> 00:25:34,016
Can't we just pull out for today?

340
00:25:34,016 --> 00:25:36,200
Come on, what have you even done? Get up.

341
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:39,749
Even if we're pulling out,
we should at least ring the doorbell first.

342
00:25:44,583 --> 00:25:47,283
Wait, hold up!

343
00:25:49,256 --> 00:25:51,068
Please don't misunderstand
the current situation.

344
00:25:51,068 --> 00:25:52,283
The employees downstairs

345
00:25:52,283 --> 00:25:54,116
- are completely innocent.
- Shh!

346
00:25:56,528 --> 00:25:59,752
Don't do anything else.
Just go straight down to the first floor.

347
00:25:59,752 --> 00:26:03,083
If you leave the building now,
I'll pretend I never saw you.

348
00:26:09,116 --> 00:26:10,816
What was that?

349
00:26:13,044 --> 00:26:14,630
Darn it!

350
00:26:14,630 --> 00:26:16,483
Seriously...

351
00:26:19,183 --> 00:26:23,604
You're good at scurrying away like a rat.

352
00:26:23,604 --> 00:26:26,998
How long are you going to keep blocking me?

353
00:26:26,998 --> 00:26:31,149
Oh... Is blocking all you can do?

354
00:26:31,856 --> 00:26:33,130
Curious?

355
00:26:33,130 --> 00:26:34,830
You!

356
00:26:45,736 --> 00:26:48,083
Then try blocking me yourself.

357
00:27:04,472 --> 00:27:07,983
What are you? What kind of woman are you?

358
00:27:09,928 --> 00:27:11,783
The water stopped.

359
00:27:18,483 --> 00:27:21,383
Director Yoo Bo Na, it's me!

360
00:27:22,144 --> 00:27:23,844
You...

361
00:27:30,268 --> 00:27:34,476
<i>♪ Dun-da, Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪</i>

362
00:27:34,476 --> 00:27:38,016
<i>♪ In those four beats ♪</i>

363
00:27:44,904 --> 00:27:46,900
Oh, yeah, Secretary Kim.

364
00:27:46,900 --> 00:27:50,300
After that soak, I'm getting a little hungry.

365
00:27:50,300 --> 00:27:53,183
Shall I grab a bite before heading down?

366
00:27:53,835 --> 00:27:56,164
Alright, alright.

367
00:27:56,164 --> 00:28:01,040
<i>♪ There is love, and there is farewell ♪</i>

368
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:04,883
<i>♪ And there are tears too ♪</i>

369
00:28:08,049 --> 00:28:11,749
What a spectacular day this has been.

370
00:28:11,749 --> 00:28:13,836
How are your nerves holding up?

371
00:28:13,836 --> 00:28:16,424
You're scared out of your wits.

372
00:28:16,424 --> 00:28:20,316
I didn't know meeting one person
could be this hard.

373
00:28:25,204 --> 00:28:27,816
It's like a giant fortress.

374
00:28:28,676 --> 00:28:31,149
Like a solid castle wall.

375
00:28:31,149 --> 00:28:32,716
It does.

376
00:28:32,716 --> 00:28:36,505
In movies, places that look this glamorous

377
00:28:36,505 --> 00:28:40,049
usually have some dark secret
lurking underneath.

378
00:28:40,812 --> 00:28:44,516
Eventually, those secrets
always come to light.

379
00:28:45,583 --> 00:28:48,549
That's what people like us are here for.

380
00:28:51,716 --> 00:28:52,716
Nice to meet you.

381
00:28:52,716 --> 00:28:55,072
I'm Bae Bi Ji, owner of Dalsam Auto.

382
00:28:55,072 --> 00:28:59,768
Hello. I'm Go Yeong Gap, Manager of
Sales Team 3 at Durumi Electronics.

383
00:28:59,768 --> 00:29:04,692
Oh, and this is our team hacker,
Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do.

384
00:29:04,692 --> 00:29:06,983
A hacker?

385
00:29:06,983 --> 00:29:10,477
So the CCTV going down was his doing.

386
00:29:10,477 --> 00:29:14,568
I've heard there are separate teams
for different regions and assignments,

387
00:29:14,568 --> 00:29:16,168
but this is my first time
meeting you in person.

388
00:29:16,168 --> 00:29:17,576
Well, unless something unexpected
like this happens,

389
00:29:17,576 --> 00:29:19,749
we don't really cross paths.

390
00:29:20,724 --> 00:29:21,880
Oh, and this is...

391
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:24,390
Oh, no need to introduce her.
I know her well.

392
00:29:24,390 --> 00:29:28,249
Is there anyone in this line of work
who doesn't know Director Yoo?

393
00:29:28,916 --> 00:29:30,900
I've met her before too.

394
00:29:30,900 --> 00:29:32,749
Back when Ms. Bae was team leader.

395
00:29:33,618 --> 00:29:34,952
Yeah.

396
00:29:34,952 --> 00:29:37,949
You were just a rookie back then.
You're a team leader already?

397
00:29:38,608 --> 00:29:42,149
Well, it wasn't exactly intentional.
There's a bit of a story behind it.

398
00:29:42,804 --> 00:29:44,540
Oh, these are our employees.

399
00:29:44,540 --> 00:29:46,928
This is Ms. Mun Meo Ru,
who mainly works in the field.

400
00:29:46,928 --> 00:29:50,732
Wow, it's a miracle she survived
going up against you, Director Yoo.

401
00:29:50,732 --> 00:29:52,742
Didn't you go a little easy on her?

402
00:29:52,742 --> 00:29:54,014
What? She was pretty good.

403
00:29:54,014 --> 00:29:57,168
Though she does seem a little reckless.

404
00:29:57,168 --> 00:30:01,449
Yes, well, thank you for sparing me.

405
00:30:05,096 --> 00:30:09,748
And this is our team's idea machine,
our part-timer, Ms. Mun Da Rae.

406
00:30:09,748 --> 00:30:12,464
Oh, it's cold.

407
00:30:12,464 --> 00:30:16,016
She seems to have the most experience,
but her position is still just part-time.

408
00:30:16,016 --> 00:30:19,424
She really hates being
responsible for anything.

409
00:30:19,424 --> 00:30:20,812
You know me, right?

410
00:30:20,812 --> 00:30:22,277
We met at the casino earlier.

411
00:30:22,277 --> 00:30:25,316
I know you, chicken heart.

412
00:30:26,355 --> 00:30:28,056
But how did you pull that off?

413
00:30:28,056 --> 00:30:31,812
You had a higher win rate
than the program I designed.

414
00:30:31,812 --> 00:30:34,080
Use your brain, your brain.

415
00:30:34,080 --> 00:30:38,231
You stupidly cling to machines,
so you get outsmarted that stupidly.

416
00:30:38,231 --> 00:30:40,216
Oh, dear, I'm sorry.

417
00:30:41,352 --> 00:30:45,116
Our part-timer is brilliant,
but she's a little lacking in social skills.

418
00:30:47,852 --> 00:30:50,557
Then shall we hear about your client?

419
00:30:50,557 --> 00:30:53,683
Oh, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil?

420
00:30:54,356 --> 00:30:56,976
In a nutshell, he's a serial sexual predator.

421
00:30:56,976 --> 00:30:58,880
He was caught red-handed a few years ago,

422
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:01,304
but got away with a suspended sentence.

423
00:31:01,304 --> 00:31:05,684
<i>He hired the wife of one of his
construction workers as a housekeeper,</i>

424
00:31:05,684 --> 00:31:09,372
<i>and repeatedly sexually assaulted her
by threatening her husband's job.</i>

425
00:31:09,372 --> 00:31:10,840
Her husband found out

426
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:14,716
and threatened to go to the press
unless he confessed.

427
00:31:14,716 --> 00:31:18,668
<i>So, Chairman Cheon bribed
a fellow worker with a criminal record</i>

428
00:31:18,668 --> 00:31:20,528
<i>and had him murder the husband.</i>

429
00:31:20,528 --> 00:31:22,296
<i>Then he covered it up by staging the murder</i>

430
00:31:22,296 --> 00:31:25,944
<i>as an accidental fall caused by
the victim's own negligence.</i>

431
00:31:25,944 --> 00:31:28,516
Help me! Please!

432
00:31:28,516 --> 00:31:31,727
Save me! I was wrong.
I said I was wrong. Please save me.

433
00:31:31,727 --> 00:31:34,172
<i>We just met with the coworker</i>

434
00:31:34,172 --> 00:31:36,549
<i>who was hired
to kill the husband a few days ago.</i>

435
00:31:38,376 --> 00:31:43,549
Chairman Cheon must be thrilled that
the guy who had dirt on him is dead.

436
00:31:45,416 --> 00:31:46,416
Oh, right!

437
00:31:46,416 --> 00:31:50,571
I think two reporters were following
Chairman Cheon earlier.

438
00:31:50,571 --> 00:31:51,685
Reporters?

439
00:31:51,685 --> 00:31:54,104
The media lost interest quickly

440
00:31:54,104 --> 00:31:56,200
because Chairman Cheon
cleverly covered up the case.

441
00:31:56,200 --> 00:32:00,680
So I thought it was interesting that
reporters are still digging into it.

442
00:32:00,680 --> 00:32:02,949
They seemed pretty persistent.

443
00:32:02,949 --> 00:32:06,976
I sent them away because it seemed dangerous
if they kept getting closer,

444
00:32:06,976 --> 00:32:08,849
but I'm not sure if they've actually left.

445
00:32:12,916 --> 00:32:14,749
Yul, I'll close the door. Watch your hand.

446
00:32:16,452 --> 00:32:19,068
But, honey, are you
really sure you have time?

447
00:32:19,068 --> 00:32:22,112
If you think it might be tough,
should we quickly ask Se Ah now?

448
00:32:22,112 --> 00:32:25,776
I do have an interview
a little farther away...

449
00:32:25,776 --> 00:32:27,252
But I should be fine. I can make it on time.

450
00:32:27,252 --> 00:32:29,692
Bad guys don't usually give you much time.

451
00:32:29,692 --> 00:32:31,172
Yeah? A bad guy?

452
00:32:31,172 --> 00:32:33,149
How bad is this guy?

453
00:32:34,235 --> 00:32:38,683
On the surface, it looks like an accident,
but a premeditated murder underneath?

454
00:32:38,683 --> 00:32:42,249
I'm going to expose the person
who ordered it and make sure he pays.

455
00:32:47,984 --> 00:32:50,132
So why did you go after Tak Jong Gu?

456
00:32:50,132 --> 00:32:53,984
We were looking for a fool
who could get us onto the VIP floor.

457
00:32:53,984 --> 00:32:57,877
We planned to set that room on fire
and sneak into Cheon Seong Gil's room

458
00:32:57,877 --> 00:32:59,883
during the chaos for the meeting.

459
00:33:00,592 --> 00:33:02,449
You came up with
quite a complicated scenario.

460
00:33:02,449 --> 00:33:07,757
Coming all the way to a casino,
and even playing games yourself to do it?

461
00:33:07,757 --> 00:33:12,116
She just made it fit
because she wanted to gamble.

462
00:33:14,524 --> 00:33:17,128
Anyway, they weren't even
particularly difficult meetings,

463
00:33:17,128 --> 00:33:19,460
but since our dates and routes overlapped,

464
00:33:19,460 --> 00:33:22,216
we ended up unintentionally
interfering with each other.

465
00:33:24,416 --> 00:33:29,316
Since we're already in this together,
how about we work together this time?

466
00:33:30,756 --> 00:33:33,083
Well, sounds like a good idea.

467
00:33:33,083 --> 00:33:36,783
- I'm in.
- If Ms. Yoo is okay with it, I'm fine too.

468
00:33:37,796 --> 00:33:43,784
We've never worked together before,
so we don't know each other's styles.

469
00:33:43,784 --> 00:33:45,456
Isn't this a bit of a gamble?

470
00:33:45,456 --> 00:33:47,940
Oh, I like a gamble.

471
00:33:47,940 --> 00:33:49,596
- I'm in!
- I'm against it.

472
00:33:49,596 --> 00:33:51,000
I'm not feeling great.

473
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:52,944
Well, looks like the vote went in favor.

474
00:33:52,944 --> 00:33:54,368
Let's do the collaboration.

475
00:33:54,368 --> 00:33:57,616
Jeez, she always does whatever she wants.

476
00:34:00,383 --> 00:34:02,424
Yeah, we should.

477
00:34:02,424 --> 00:34:05,483
Our part-timer is a bit of a dictator.

478
00:34:07,104 --> 00:34:09,568
But we have to wrap up the meeting
by tomorrow.

479
00:34:09,568 --> 00:34:12,460
Do we have time to rework the scenario?

480
00:34:12,460 --> 00:34:13,649
Why drag it out till tomorrow?

481
00:34:13,649 --> 00:34:16,016
We've already got the whole story.

482
00:34:16,016 --> 00:34:18,468
For this one...

483
00:34:18,468 --> 00:34:20,561
let's go with Go-Stop.

484
00:34:20,561 --> 00:34:24,216
Kill two birds with one stone.

485
00:34:24,216 --> 00:34:28,176
<i>Isn't it risky to meet Tak Jong Gu again?</i>

486
00:34:28,176 --> 00:34:29,983
<i>If he finds out we drugged him...</i>

487
00:34:31,456 --> 00:34:32,748
All mine!

488
00:34:32,748 --> 00:34:34,296
<i>He's a junkie.</i>

489
00:34:34,296 --> 00:34:35,888
<i>He'll think the wine was switched by mistake</i>

490
00:34:35,888 --> 00:34:38,100
<i>and that he drank his own drugged wine.</i>

491
00:34:38,100 --> 00:34:39,227
What?

492
00:34:39,227 --> 00:34:40,600
I thought you'd left. You're still here?

493
00:34:40,600 --> 00:34:42,551
I got a room too.

494
00:34:42,551 --> 00:34:44,516
Are you sober now?

495
00:34:44,516 --> 00:34:45,924
Yeah.

496
00:34:45,924 --> 00:34:51,916
Well, I'm usually a heavy drinker,
but one lousy drink knocked me out.

497
00:34:52,620 --> 00:34:55,183
Anyway, good to see you again.

498
00:34:55,183 --> 00:34:57,583
Oh, this is boring.

499
00:34:57,583 --> 00:34:59,676
Why is there no thrill in this?

500
00:34:59,676 --> 00:35:02,749
I'm not feeling any dopamine.

501
00:35:04,312 --> 00:35:06,704
Want to come back to my room?

502
00:35:06,704 --> 00:35:09,248
I've got something seriously killer.

503
00:35:09,248 --> 00:35:14,092
You pathetic junkie prick who thinks
your rich dad makes you untouchable.

504
00:35:14,092 --> 00:35:15,092
What?

505
00:35:15,092 --> 00:35:17,524
Someone said that about you.

506
00:35:17,524 --> 00:35:18,724
Is that true?

507
00:35:18,724 --> 00:35:20,536
Who said that?

508
00:35:20,536 --> 00:35:23,220
Which punk talked nonsense like that?

509
00:35:23,220 --> 00:35:25,441
Over there...

510
00:35:25,441 --> 00:35:27,616
some old guy with a big belly.

511
00:35:28,740 --> 00:35:30,628
Your name is Tak Jong Gu, right?

512
00:35:30,628 --> 00:35:32,520
I heard he's some chairman.

513
00:35:32,520 --> 00:35:35,888
Oh, Gaecheon Construction?

514
00:35:35,888 --> 00:35:37,460
Gaecheon?

515
00:35:37,460 --> 00:35:39,272
Has the old man lost his mind?

516
00:35:39,272 --> 00:35:41,016
Give me a good hand.

517
00:35:44,376 --> 00:35:46,569
Oh, my, what is this?

518
00:35:46,569 --> 00:35:49,616
- Old man, have you lost your mind?
- Oh, my, what's this?

519
00:35:49,616 --> 00:35:53,268
You little punk who keeps paying off
my old man every quarter.

520
00:35:53,268 --> 00:35:55,338
You think you're untouchable, huh?

521
00:35:55,338 --> 00:35:56,649
Hey, what are you? Hey!

522
00:35:56,649 --> 00:35:58,848
- What on earth are you...
- Watch your mouth, or else, huh?

523
00:35:58,848 --> 00:36:01,268
Maybe you'll come to your senses
when your company goes under.

524
00:36:01,268 --> 00:36:02,676
Darn it!

525
00:36:02,676 --> 00:36:04,376
Hey!

526
00:36:06,552 --> 00:36:10,764
- What are you?
- <i>That should be enough witnesses.</i>

527
00:36:10,764 --> 00:36:13,576
- <i>What's next?</i>
- Wow...

528
00:36:13,576 --> 00:36:17,316
I really like that
you're a total punk, Jong Gu.

529
00:36:19,784 --> 00:36:22,249
That killer stuff you mentioned earlier...

530
00:36:23,008 --> 00:36:24,749
is that offer still good?

531
00:36:27,860 --> 00:36:29,560
Are you interested in that?

532
00:36:30,176 --> 00:36:31,916
Of course, it is.

533
00:36:33,004 --> 00:36:35,849
One dose, and you're off to heaven.

534
00:36:38,452 --> 00:36:40,780
Bring that to my room in an hour.

535
00:36:40,780 --> 00:36:43,349
Without anyone knowing.

536
00:36:48,868 --> 00:36:54,572
When Tak Jong Gu walks into the room
and finds Chairman Cheon dead,

537
00:36:54,572 --> 00:36:56,883
he'll be shocked into passing out.

538
00:36:56,883 --> 00:37:02,236
Yeah, we'll give the unconscious guy
the drug we brought first.

539
00:37:02,236 --> 00:37:06,632
Then Team A can go in
and finish off Tak Jong Gu.

540
00:37:06,632 --> 00:37:07,992
Bingo!

541
00:37:07,992 --> 00:37:12,662
Tak Jong Gu, still furious even after
causing that scene in the gaming room,

542
00:37:12,662 --> 00:37:15,352
takes a full dose of drugs, loses his mind,

543
00:37:15,352 --> 00:37:17,540
and storms into Cheon Seong Gil's room.

544
00:37:17,540 --> 00:37:19,449
We'll take him out first.

545
00:37:19,449 --> 00:37:24,676
Then he'll throw himself
out the window. Boom!

546
00:37:24,676 --> 00:37:26,376
Done.

547
00:37:37,649 --> 00:37:39,849
[Big Precious]

548
00:37:42,316 --> 00:37:45,149
Honey, I'm on my way to pick up Yul.
I'm almost there.

549
00:37:45,149 --> 00:37:46,847
Are you going to Seo Yeon's place now?

550
00:37:46,847 --> 00:37:48,520
I'm sorry, I'm a bit late, right?

551
00:37:48,520 --> 00:37:51,608
But I called ahead to let them know.

552
00:37:51,608 --> 00:37:53,506
No, I'm not nagging you.

553
00:37:53,506 --> 00:37:55,180
<i>Have you eaten?</i>

554
00:37:55,180 --> 00:37:58,356
I can just eat at home later.
What about you, honey?

555
00:37:58,356 --> 00:38:00,988
Well, I grabbed something quick.

556
00:38:00,988 --> 00:38:03,792
I'm still out. I haven't finished work yet.

557
00:38:03,792 --> 00:38:05,308
Still?

558
00:38:05,308 --> 00:38:08,504
Didn't you have a client meeting today?
Did it not go well?

559
00:38:08,504 --> 00:38:13,116
Oh, the meeting fell through this afternoon,
so it got pushed to tonight.

560
00:38:14,056 --> 00:38:16,920
Did the interview with the bad guy go well?

561
00:38:16,920 --> 00:38:18,580
<i>Me? Well...</i>

562
00:38:18,580 --> 00:38:20,704
It's not like I had an appointment with him.

563
00:38:20,704 --> 00:38:25,100
And bad guys don't usually
give interviews willingly, you know.

564
00:38:25,100 --> 00:38:26,100
<i>Then what do I do?</i>

565
00:38:26,100 --> 00:38:27,768
I just have to barge in.

566
00:38:27,768 --> 00:38:29,392
So, did you meet him?

567
00:38:29,392 --> 00:38:33,484
I did meet him,
but I got kicked out right away.

568
00:38:33,484 --> 00:38:35,748
I couldn't even ask one question.

569
00:38:35,748 --> 00:38:37,484
Oh, I see.

570
00:38:37,484 --> 00:38:40,684
It's okay. I'll just barge in again tomorrow.

571
00:38:40,684 --> 00:38:42,344
Honey, I'm almost there.

572
00:38:42,344 --> 00:38:43,716
<i>Can we talk again later?</i>

573
00:38:43,716 --> 00:38:44,749
Yul's probably waiting.

574
00:38:44,749 --> 00:38:45,849
<i>Yeah, okay.</i>

575
00:38:45,849 --> 00:38:47,424
Make sure you eat.

576
00:38:47,424 --> 00:38:49,124
<i>Okay.</i>

577
00:39:01,360 --> 00:39:05,149
Tak Jong Gu's actions are not deviating
from expectations one bit.

578
00:39:05,149 --> 00:39:08,216
Everything went according to plan
up to the gaming room.

579
00:39:08,912 --> 00:39:10,612
Yeah.

580
00:39:11,988 --> 00:39:14,308
You've seemed a little off, Ms. Yoo.

581
00:39:14,308 --> 00:39:17,016
Is something bothering you?

582
00:39:19,989 --> 00:39:22,630
I saw my husband at the casino earlier.

583
00:39:22,630 --> 00:39:24,330
Your husband?

584
00:39:26,580 --> 00:39:29,716
<i>Then that man I saw earlier was...</i>

585
00:39:29,716 --> 00:39:31,564
I'll find out where he is right now.

586
00:39:31,564 --> 00:39:33,110
I just talked to him on the phone.

587
00:39:33,110 --> 00:39:34,664
He said he's on his way home.

588
00:39:34,664 --> 00:39:37,016
We won't run into each other anymore.

589
00:39:38,548 --> 00:39:41,949
But your husband being here...

590
00:39:43,196 --> 00:39:45,149
Could it be that gambling...

591
00:39:46,264 --> 00:39:48,049
That can't be right.

592
00:39:48,840 --> 00:39:50,648
Sorry.

593
00:39:50,648 --> 00:39:53,976
He said he had an interview
out of town today.

594
00:39:53,976 --> 00:39:56,312
But I didn't expect him to be here.

595
00:39:56,312 --> 00:39:58,749
An interview, with whom?

596
00:39:58,749 --> 00:40:02,416
Oh, the reporter who's digging into
Chairman Cheon...

597
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:06,812
Let's get to work.

598
00:40:06,812 --> 00:40:09,609
Where are the two of them now?

599
00:40:09,609 --> 00:40:13,784
Okay, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
just went into his room,

600
00:40:13,784 --> 00:40:16,904
and Tak Jong Gu went into his room too.

601
00:40:16,904 --> 00:40:18,832
Then the timing should work.

602
00:40:18,832 --> 00:40:21,049
Okay, shall we go?

603
00:40:22,608 --> 00:40:24,308
Ms. Yoo.

604
00:40:25,764 --> 00:40:28,056
Never leave me out again.

605
00:40:28,056 --> 00:40:30,668
That won't happen again, okay?

606
00:40:30,668 --> 00:40:32,368
I'm going.

607
00:41:00,264 --> 00:41:01,724
Wow!

608
00:41:01,724 --> 00:41:03,424
Nice room!

609
00:41:06,904 --> 00:41:10,398
My baby, where are you?

610
00:41:10,398 --> 00:41:12,808
Are you getting ready for something special?

611
00:41:12,808 --> 00:41:15,083
I love the outfit you had on earlier.

612
00:41:25,724 --> 00:41:29,232
That darn punk made me shower again.

613
00:41:29,232 --> 00:41:31,680
I'm so annoyed.

614
00:41:31,680 --> 00:41:34,149
Oh, my, so annoying.

615
00:41:35,788 --> 00:41:37,444
What? Who are you?

616
00:41:37,444 --> 00:41:39,683
Who are you? Huh?

617
00:41:42,996 --> 00:41:46,148
You little punk, you...

618
00:41:46,148 --> 00:41:48,792
Why on earth are you here?

619
00:41:48,792 --> 00:41:50,876
What are you doing in my woman's room?

620
00:41:50,876 --> 00:41:54,516
Jeez, you punk, you're in for it now.

621
00:41:54,516 --> 00:41:58,924
Get over here! You punk!

622
00:41:58,924 --> 00:42:00,416
Punk?

623
00:42:00,416 --> 00:42:02,849
Should I tear you apart?

624
00:42:15,508 --> 00:42:16,896
You two make quite a pair.

625
00:42:16,896 --> 00:42:19,516
I think there's a simpler way,
don't you think?

626
00:42:19,516 --> 00:42:24,852
I saw a small light outside
Chairman Cheon's room window.

627
00:42:24,852 --> 00:42:29,212
You're good at scurrying away like a rat.

628
00:42:29,212 --> 00:42:31,583
How long are you going to keep blocking me?

629
00:42:32,683 --> 00:42:34,983
If I'm right...

630
00:42:38,836 --> 00:42:40,536
You're right.

631
00:42:41,749 --> 00:42:45,600
<i>Cheon Seong Gil's room and Tak Jong Gu's room
are on the opposite rear line.</i>

632
00:42:45,600 --> 00:42:47,716
<i>Outside those windows,
there are two mountains on either end,</i>

633
00:42:47,716 --> 00:42:51,984
<i>and a cable car is running
back and forth between them.</i>

634
00:42:51,984 --> 00:42:53,684
Then...

635
00:42:55,684 --> 00:42:59,640
As things stand, everyone here
could be called in by the police

636
00:42:59,640 --> 00:43:01,384
during the investigation.

637
00:43:01,384 --> 00:43:06,592
Especially those who had direct contact
with Cheon Seong Gil and Tak Jong Gu.

638
00:43:06,592 --> 00:43:08,288
There'll be plenty of witnesses.

639
00:43:08,288 --> 00:43:11,292
Let's just take the long way
and kill two birds with one stone, yeah?

640
00:43:11,292 --> 00:43:12,992
You're right.

641
00:43:17,883 --> 00:43:18,964
Hey, you punk!

642
00:43:18,964 --> 00:43:22,136
How dare some young punk
talk to an adult like that?

643
00:43:22,136 --> 00:43:25,952
Darn it! Hey! You want me
to chop your hand off?

644
00:43:25,952 --> 00:43:28,220
You ungrateful punk!

645
00:43:28,220 --> 00:43:29,748
I've been letting you get away with it,
but now you've gone too far!

646
00:43:29,748 --> 00:43:32,896
- Give it to me!
- Hand it over!

647
00:43:32,896 --> 00:43:35,372
I'll make you go through exactly
what I went through.

648
00:43:35,372 --> 00:43:36,676
Why won't this open?

649
00:43:36,676 --> 00:43:40,600
Hey, that's expensive, okay?

650
00:43:40,600 --> 00:43:41,849
Give that up, you old geezer!

651
00:43:41,849 --> 00:43:43,516
What?

652
00:43:43,516 --> 00:43:45,644
What? You little...

653
00:43:45,644 --> 00:43:48,024
What? Old geezer?

654
00:43:48,024 --> 00:43:50,308
Darn it!

655
00:43:50,308 --> 00:43:52,548
Old geezer! Old geezer!

656
00:43:52,548 --> 00:43:54,449
Okay, shall we go?

657
00:44:29,628 --> 00:44:31,616
Give it back! It's mine!

658
00:44:57,968 --> 00:45:00,783
One-two, client meeting completed.

659
00:45:17,104 --> 00:45:20,004
Alright, good work, everyone.

660
00:45:20,004 --> 00:45:22,984
Get some good rest tomorrow,
and I'll see you all the day after.

661
00:45:22,984 --> 00:45:24,684
Yeah.

662
00:45:29,916 --> 00:45:34,192
I wish I'd gotten to see
that historic moment with my own eyes.

663
00:45:34,192 --> 00:45:35,749
At least we saved the cost of a bullet.

664
00:45:35,749 --> 00:45:38,604
Our operating expenses were already tight.

665
00:45:38,604 --> 00:45:43,652
But I never knew there were people
in the area doing the same thing.

666
00:45:43,652 --> 00:45:48,449
There are too many bad guys in the world
for us to handle them all ourselves.

667
00:45:52,484 --> 00:45:54,449
Rest in peace, everyone.

668
00:45:55,604 --> 00:45:57,783
You two are headed the same way,

669
00:45:58,856 --> 00:46:01,016
so at least you won't be bored.

670
00:46:06,867 --> 00:46:09,916
Is our Tae Soon thirsty?

671
00:46:09,916 --> 00:46:14,220
Oh, alright. I'll give you some more water.

672
00:46:14,220 --> 00:46:18,548
Drink plenty of water,
and let's live together for a long time.

673
00:46:18,548 --> 00:46:22,049
I'll even get you another supplement
for your birthday this year.

674
00:46:24,894 --> 00:46:27,749
Looks like someone made Yoo Bo Na mad.

675
00:46:28,768 --> 00:46:31,849
No, it's nothing. Not you.
I mean, your owner.

676
00:46:31,849 --> 00:46:35,049
Yeah, want some more water?

677
00:46:35,049 --> 00:46:36,749
Yeah.

678
00:46:39,656 --> 00:46:41,849
Oh, my, so pretty!

679
00:46:41,849 --> 00:46:44,549
Alright, alright.

680
00:46:48,472 --> 00:46:50,968
Wow, as expected of Kingfisher.

681
00:46:50,968 --> 00:46:55,349
I finally got to meet the legend I've only
heard about. Today is my lucky day.

682
00:46:55,999 --> 00:46:56,999
You happy?

683
00:46:56,999 --> 00:47:00,748
What's so exciting about
getting carried by someone else?

684
00:47:00,748 --> 00:47:04,249
At least we won't
be getting called in by the police.

685
00:47:04,249 --> 00:47:07,249
There's no more perfect alibi than this.

686
00:47:08,236 --> 00:47:11,768
Hey, we're done for the day,
so let's go get some drinks.

687
00:47:11,768 --> 00:47:14,949
A day like this calls for chicken and beer.

688
00:47:16,380 --> 00:47:18,632
It's on me today.

689
00:47:18,632 --> 00:47:21,316
Ah, on me, on me!

690
00:47:22,088 --> 00:47:24,148
She looks the happiest of all.

691
00:47:24,148 --> 00:47:26,456
No, she's scared right now.

692
00:47:26,456 --> 00:47:30,204
She's just pretending to be tough.

693
00:47:30,204 --> 00:47:31,816
Hey, why don't you quit gambling
while you're at it?

694
00:47:31,816 --> 00:47:36,844
Hurry up! Whoever's late has to
write their name with their butt!

695
00:47:36,844 --> 00:47:39,583
Da Rae, I'll just be late!

696
00:47:40,380 --> 00:47:41,772
Oh, how embarrassing.

697
00:47:41,772 --> 00:47:45,728
Oh, this is so humiliating. Oh, I hate this.

698
00:47:45,728 --> 00:47:47,816
Oh, being the boss is really hard.

699
00:47:47,816 --> 00:47:49,649
What's wrong with him?

700
00:47:52,884 --> 00:47:54,332
Daddy, why isn't Mommy here?

701
00:47:54,332 --> 00:47:57,102
I told you Mommy was staying the night.

702
00:47:57,102 --> 00:48:00,616
If Yul goes to sleep
and goes to daycare tomorrow,

703
00:48:00,616 --> 00:48:03,308
Mommy will be there to greet you with, "Yul!"

704
00:48:03,308 --> 00:48:05,260
But where did Mommy go?

705
00:48:05,260 --> 00:48:07,136
She went to work.

706
00:48:07,136 --> 00:48:08,880
Hmm... Something important?

707
00:48:08,880 --> 00:48:11,849
Huh? What kind of work?

708
00:48:13,323 --> 00:48:16,604
Wait, wait.

709
00:48:16,604 --> 00:48:19,349
Sit down here for a minute. Have a seat.

710
00:48:22,051 --> 00:48:24,244
Oh, Ms. Gu, did you get home okay?

711
00:48:24,244 --> 00:48:25,244
What made you call this late?

712
00:48:25,244 --> 00:48:28,996
Mr. Kwon, did you see the breaking news?

713
00:48:28,996 --> 00:48:30,536
Breaking news?

714
00:48:30,536 --> 00:48:32,836
What is it? But what's wrong with your voice?

715
00:48:32,836 --> 00:48:37,092
Chairman Cheon Seong Gil... is dead.
He was shot by Kingfisher.

716
00:48:37,092 --> 00:48:38,884
What?

717
00:48:38,884 --> 00:48:41,496
<i>Two guests were shot and killed</i>

718
00:48:41,496 --> 00:48:45,356
<i>by a sniper in a VIP suite
at a casino hotel this evening.</i>

719
00:48:45,356 --> 00:48:50,200
<i>Police are leaning toward Kingfisher
being behind this attack as well.</i>

720
00:48:50,200 --> 00:48:51,688
[Kingfisher Strikes Again]
<i>This is the first time</i>

721
00:48:51,688 --> 00:48:54,387
[Two Casino VIP Guests Killed]
<i>two people have been killed</i>

722
00:48:54,387 --> 00:48:55,696
<i>in a single Kingfisher case.</i>

723
00:48:55,696 --> 00:48:59,468
<i>The victims include Chairman Cheon,
head of a major Gangwon construction firm,</i>

724
00:48:59,468 --> 00:49:02,283
<i>and Mr. Tak, the son of a five-term lawmaker.</i>

725
00:49:02,283 --> 00:49:04,336
<i>The two men were together
in Chairman Cheon's room</i>

726
00:49:04,336 --> 00:49:06,600
<i>when a single bullet
fired from outside the window</i>

727
00:49:06,600 --> 00:49:10,616
- <i>instantly killed them both.</i>
- <i>Chairman Cheon is Cheon Seong Gil, right?</i>

728
00:49:10,616 --> 00:49:12,228
This can't be happening.

729
00:49:12,228 --> 00:49:13,816
What's all this?

730
00:49:13,816 --> 00:49:16,283
And who's this Mr. Tak
who was killed with him?

731
00:49:16,283 --> 00:49:17,876
<i>Accordingly, the sniper's point of origin...</i>

732
00:49:17,876 --> 00:49:19,449
It's someone I know.

733
00:49:19,449 --> 00:49:20,649
<i>Pardon?</i>

734
00:49:20,649 --> 00:49:23,549
Do you know him? Who is he?

735
00:49:23,549 --> 00:49:27,364
The son of Assemblyman Tak Geun Soo,
Tak Jong Gu.

736
00:49:27,364 --> 00:49:30,924
<i>Given the low-lying hills
outside the windows,</i>

737
00:49:30,924 --> 00:49:33,816
<i>investigators will need to determine</i>

738
00:49:33,816 --> 00:49:35,816
- <i>where Kingfisher carried out the attack.</i>
- Ah, I wanted a chicken leg,

739
00:49:35,816 --> 00:49:36,976
but they're already sold out.

740
00:49:36,976 --> 00:49:38,716
They're really popular these days.

741
00:49:38,716 --> 00:49:42,092
Instead, I got you this fish cake bar
and the cream bread you like.

742
00:49:42,092 --> 00:49:43,952
And I got two sweet Choco Pies.

743
00:49:43,952 --> 00:49:45,184
Here you go!

744
00:49:45,184 --> 00:49:46,884
And some hot coffee!

745
00:49:47,936 --> 00:49:50,883
You were always lecturing me about
not using my phone while we're on stakeout.

746
00:49:50,883 --> 00:49:52,432
So what could be so interesting?

747
00:49:52,432 --> 00:49:54,132
Shh!

748
00:49:56,283 --> 00:49:58,112
[Two Victims Shot with a Single Bullet]

749
00:49:58,112 --> 00:50:01,249
What's this? Kingfisher struck again already?

750
00:50:03,600 --> 00:50:04,912
Two people?

751
00:50:04,912 --> 00:50:06,540
With one bullet?

752
00:50:06,540 --> 00:50:08,176
So, what is it? One shot, two kills?

753
00:50:08,176 --> 00:50:11,216
- Amazing!
- Hey, you're making a racket.

754
00:50:12,196 --> 00:50:13,196
Where are we going?

755
00:50:13,196 --> 00:50:15,352
We're in the middle of a stakeout, aren't we?

756
00:50:15,352 --> 00:50:18,028
Mr. Jang is going to take over.
He'll be here soon.

757
00:50:18,028 --> 00:50:20,600
Oh, so where are we...

758
00:50:20,600 --> 00:50:21,649
[Hongseon Casino]
Hongseon?

759
00:50:21,649 --> 00:50:24,256
A casino? At this hour?

760
00:50:24,256 --> 00:50:26,480
If we want to get footage of the scene,
we have to go now.

761
00:50:26,480 --> 00:50:27,544
Get some sleep.

762
00:50:27,544 --> 00:50:29,768
Wow, the scene of a one-shot double kill.

763
00:50:29,768 --> 00:50:33,549
But if the chief finds out about this,
we'll just get yelled at, right?

764
00:50:45,836 --> 00:50:48,488
[Five Years Ago]
The defendant, Tak Jong Gu,

765
00:50:48,488 --> 00:50:50,849
was found not guilty.

766
00:50:53,149 --> 00:50:56,164
Good work. Why did it take so long?

767
00:50:56,164 --> 00:50:57,592
No, this is unbelievable.

768
00:50:57,592 --> 00:51:01,636
How can there be a verdict like this?

769
00:51:01,636 --> 00:51:03,440
- Mom...
- My daughter is dead!

770
00:51:03,440 --> 00:51:05,383
- My sister...
- That punk killed her!

771
00:51:05,383 --> 00:51:07,924
- Mom!
- Hey!

772
00:51:07,924 --> 00:51:09,624
Mom...

773
00:51:11,424 --> 00:51:12,424
Bring my daughter back!

774
00:51:12,424 --> 00:51:15,396
How can he be found not guilty?

775
00:51:15,396 --> 00:51:18,349
Bring my daughter back!

776
00:51:18,349 --> 00:51:20,916
- Hey!
- Bring her back!

777
00:51:20,916 --> 00:51:22,932
- I said bring my daughter back!
- Mom...

778
00:51:22,932 --> 00:51:25,316
Bring my daughter back!

779
00:51:27,116 --> 00:51:29,749
[Court]

780
00:51:31,744 --> 00:51:34,883
Hey, get everyone together right now.

781
00:51:34,883 --> 00:51:37,920
What do you think? A celebration, you idiot.

782
00:51:37,920 --> 00:51:39,764
The girls?

783
00:51:39,764 --> 00:51:43,376
Of course, we should invite them.

784
00:51:43,376 --> 00:51:45,116
Yeah.

785
00:51:45,116 --> 00:51:46,292
Oh, really?

786
00:51:46,292 --> 00:51:48,983
Then should we just rent out an entire club?

787
00:51:51,784 --> 00:51:53,549
Let's go!

788
00:52:32,876 --> 00:52:35,816
Oh, Bo Na, Bo Na!

789
00:52:37,772 --> 00:52:40,060
Tae Seong!

790
00:52:40,060 --> 00:52:41,360
What brings you here at this hour?

791
00:52:41,360 --> 00:52:43,596
I came because I missed you.

792
00:52:43,596 --> 00:52:49,649
I just really wanted
to see you tonight, Bo Na.

793
00:52:52,984 --> 00:52:55,316
Have you been drinking?

794
00:52:55,316 --> 00:52:57,896
Well... a little?

795
00:52:57,896 --> 00:53:00,132
What...

796
00:53:00,132 --> 00:53:02,988
Why did you drink so much?
You can't even hold your liquor.

797
00:53:02,988 --> 00:53:05,484
That's not true. I can hold my liquor, okay?

798
00:53:05,484 --> 00:53:06,484
Tch...

799
00:53:06,484 --> 00:53:13,108
Still, I'd rather have
a strawberry shake with you.

800
00:53:13,108 --> 00:53:16,616
Cheers! Your favorite strawberry shake.

801
00:53:21,104 --> 00:53:26,132
But today, I just... drank like this.

802
00:53:26,132 --> 00:53:31,316
I drank because the only thing
I could hold in my hand

803
00:53:32,200 --> 00:53:33,908
was a glass of alcohol.

804
00:53:33,908 --> 00:53:38,764
Not a gun, not a knife, not even a pen.

805
00:53:38,764 --> 00:53:42,249
So I ended up with a glass.

806
00:53:49,308 --> 00:53:52,656
Did something happen today?

807
00:53:52,656 --> 00:53:54,708
Something?

808
00:53:54,708 --> 00:53:57,024
Well, yeah...

809
00:53:57,024 --> 00:53:59,636
Something always happens.
It's an everyday thing.

810
00:53:59,636 --> 00:54:01,724
Getting slammed into walls,

811
00:54:01,724 --> 00:54:04,783
thrown to the floor,

812
00:54:05,852 --> 00:54:09,820
and having my heart...

813
00:54:09,820 --> 00:54:12,583
ripped apart?

814
00:54:15,783 --> 00:54:18,449
I don't know what else I'm supposed to do.

815
00:54:22,983 --> 00:54:26,183
Bad people should be punished.

816
00:54:27,720 --> 00:54:30,949
Truly bad people should be punished.

817
00:54:33,916 --> 00:54:35,616
But I...

818
00:54:43,476 --> 00:54:46,283
I can't do anything about it.

819
00:55:24,420 --> 00:55:26,540
Get some sleep on the way.

820
00:55:26,540 --> 00:55:29,249
What are you thinking about so hard?

821
00:55:29,249 --> 00:55:31,284
Oh, nothing.

822
00:55:31,284 --> 00:55:33,752
I was just thinking about a certain day.

823
00:55:33,752 --> 00:55:35,676
What day?

824
00:55:35,676 --> 00:55:38,149
The day my husband cried for the second time.

825
00:55:42,860 --> 00:55:45,288
Well, aren't you tired yourself?

826
00:55:45,288 --> 00:55:49,780
I told you and Manager Go
to take a day off. I can drive.

827
00:55:49,780 --> 00:55:54,104
Ms. Yoo, how could I let you go alone?

828
00:55:54,104 --> 00:55:56,416
Driving at night is dangerous.

829
00:55:59,520 --> 00:56:02,876
Oh, no... I know you're...

830
00:56:02,876 --> 00:56:05,049
an excellent driver.

831
00:56:05,672 --> 00:56:08,183
But still, today...

832
00:56:08,183 --> 00:56:09,883
What about today?

833
00:56:11,672 --> 00:56:14,276
I just couldn't bring myself
to leave you alone.

834
00:56:14,276 --> 00:56:17,984
After the scare we had earlier.

835
00:56:17,984 --> 00:56:19,816
Especially since it was because of me.

836
00:56:20,492 --> 00:56:22,683
Hey, I told you it wasn't your fault.

837
00:56:22,683 --> 00:56:25,383
Unexpected things can happen anytime.

838
00:56:27,483 --> 00:56:29,588
It was the first time, Ms. Yoo.

839
00:56:29,588 --> 00:56:32,583
The first time I was truly scared.
Especially while I was there on-site.

840
00:56:34,360 --> 00:56:36,216
Me too.

841
00:56:36,216 --> 00:56:39,049
I was scared for the first time.

842
00:56:44,132 --> 00:56:47,000
Is this because you saw your husband today?

843
00:56:47,000 --> 00:56:49,616
You seemed bothered by it the whole time.

844
00:56:50,283 --> 00:56:53,349
Why did I never think of it?

845
00:56:54,012 --> 00:56:56,983
That something like this could happen.

846
00:57:36,732 --> 00:57:39,616
It's Yoo Bo Na, my wife.

847
00:57:41,036 --> 00:57:43,316
My big precious.

848
00:57:43,316 --> 00:57:46,216
Sorry, I woke you, right?

849
00:57:47,284 --> 00:57:50,576
I thought you'd be staying the night.

850
00:57:50,576 --> 00:57:53,052
I came back early because I missed you.

851
00:57:53,052 --> 00:57:55,883
I really missed you today.

852
00:57:59,484 --> 00:58:02,483
I missed you so much too.

853
00:58:05,712 --> 00:58:09,392
I'm off tomorrow. Want to go on a date?

854
00:58:09,392 --> 00:58:11,240
Let's do that.

855
00:58:11,240 --> 00:58:15,183
Let's have the date we missed last time.

856
00:58:15,888 --> 00:58:18,816
We'll look at the sky and enjoy the scenery.

857
00:58:20,364 --> 00:58:24,083
We'll worry about what to wear
and what to eat.

858
00:58:26,680 --> 00:58:30,340
Let's just have
an ordinary day together, okay?

859
00:58:30,340 --> 00:58:32,949
Just like the day we first met.

860
00:58:34,276 --> 00:58:36,849
Just like the day we first met.

861
00:58:48,376 --> 00:58:50,512
<i>Why didn't I think of that?</i>

862
00:58:50,512 --> 00:58:52,972
<i>That he's always out there,</i>

863
00:58:52,972 --> 00:58:55,024
<i>and as long as I'm still here,</i>

864
00:58:55,024 --> 00:59:00,249
<i>we could run into each other again
someday, somewhere.</i>

865
00:59:07,516 --> 00:59:09,249
<i>Just like...</i>

866
00:59:09,249 --> 00:59:12,349
<i>the day we first met.</i>

867
00:59:56,449 --> 00:59:58,692
Back then, everyone was curious
when you came back.

868
00:59:58,692 --> 01:00:00,360
They wondered what had happened
in the meantime.

869
01:00:00,360 --> 01:00:02,316
I met Yoo Bo Na.

870
01:00:02,316 --> 01:00:03,684
Try to stay alive, at least.

871
01:00:03,684 --> 01:00:05,649
Did you save Mr. Kwon Tae Seong?

872
01:00:05,649 --> 01:00:06,649
Because I felt like it.

873
01:00:06,649 --> 01:00:08,712
Have we met before?

874
01:00:08,712 --> 01:00:12,556
How do you keep picking out exactly
the people Kingfisher targets?

875
01:00:12,556 --> 01:00:14,920
But when I think about it,
she's really something.

876
01:00:14,920 --> 01:00:16,836
How on earth has she lived her life?

877
01:00:16,836 --> 01:00:17,932
Do you know anything, Tae Seong?

878
01:00:17,932 --> 01:00:21,428
Why would Director Yoo summon us
to her home herself?

879
01:00:21,428 --> 01:00:22,476
Wait a minute.

880
01:00:22,476 --> 01:00:25,816
Could Kingfisher have killed
an innocent person by mistake?

881
01:00:25,816 --> 01:00:28,236
If an innocent person was killed,
they should be held accountable too.

882
01:00:28,236 --> 01:00:30,049
Kingfisher should be caught
and locked up too.

883
01:00:30,049 --> 01:00:32,156
I got a text from Director Yoo.

884
01:00:32,156 --> 01:00:33,208
What did she say?

885
01:00:33,208 --> 01:00:34,556
I'm quitting.

886
01:00:34,556 --> 01:00:36,616
You used to want so badly to meet Kingfisher.

887
01:00:36,616 --> 01:00:38,549
I shouldn't meet her.

888
01:00:46,473 --> 01:00:48,473
Mkv Drama
